---
# Static analysis of the hub's library and its PC build: python tools/tidy.py runs it, as CI does on each push.
# The bug-finding checks only, not style. Each one left out, and why:
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters    style: many functions take two numbers or two strings
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise                 bytes are promoted to int before masking and shifting; every value is small
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#                                           sizes and offsets are small, and the board is 32-bit
#   cert-err58-cpp, cert-int09-c            the same as throwing-static-initialization, and enum style
#   clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding
#                                           field order follows meaning; the few large tables are laid out by hand
# cert-err33-c checks only the calls whose failure can lose data: a file written, closed or renamed.
# A finding that is wrong in one place is marked there with NOLINT and the reason.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cert-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -cert-int09-c,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
CheckOptions:
  cert-err33-c.CheckedFunctions: '::fclose;::fflush;::fwrite;::fputs;::fputc;::rename'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(lib[/\\](sensorcam|s2o_proto)|src|include)[/\\]'
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
...
